T {We want to make a differential ring VCO that operates at either 1.25GHz with 4x phases
or at 2.5GHz differentially. Therefore we will need to choose devices that can operate
at that speed. The typical speed will be around fT/10.

That means we need an fT > 25-30. 
	-> 0.6 < Vgs < 0.8
	-> 7 < gm/Id < 10} 230 -760 0 0 0.4 0.4 {}
T {We expect to see a gm/gds of ~20} 1320 -790 0 0 0.4 0.4 {}
T {We want to bias the devices to have a current density between 250 uA/um - 700 uA/um} 250 -80 0 0 0.4 0.4 {}
T {f_osc = 1/2pi * sqrt(gmn1^2 - (Gds + gmp2 - gmp1)^2)/CL

We want f_osc = 2.5G ~ gmn1/(2pi*CL)

CL ~ 4x NMOS Cgg ~ 0.8 fF/um} 1250 -520 0 0 0.4 0.4 {}
T {2.5GHz*2*pi = gmn1/(4x0.8 fF/um)

We also know that gm/Id ~ 7-10 and Id/W ~ 250 uA/um - 700 uA/um. 
Therefore gm/W ~ 7 uS/uA * 700 uA/um = 4900 uS/um
             to 10 uS/uA * 250 uA/um = 2500 uS/um
} 1220.861054955148 -326.1219148944668 0 0 0.4 0.4 {}
